      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Exams frequently test the classification of bodies: NITI Aayog is an Executive Body, whereas NHRC is a Statutory Body.",
        "Memorize exact Articles: CAG (Article 148), UPSC (Article 315), Election Commission (Article 324), Finance Commission (Article 280).",
        "Pay attention to mandatory qualifications, removal processes, and appointing authorities across different bodies."
      ],
      "id": "x7cb7pc"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional bodies derive their powers, status, and authority directly from the Constitution of India.",
        "Statutory bodies are created by specific Acts passed by Parliament or State Legislatures.",
        "Executive bodies are established through executive resolutions or cabinet decisions without legislative enactment.",
        "Amending the status or structure of a constitutional body requires a Constitutional Amendment Act under Article 368."
      ],
